id: dragon-like
name: Dragon-like
order: 1
category: body
# A Factor Trait replaces a Secondary Racial Trait - Secondary, then, unless it names a Primary one to replace.
importance: secondary
# (1) Up to two Bestial Traits, chosen as it is gained ("Later, by hand" for fewer) - in the Other Traits list, gone with it.
grantsOther: bestial
grantsOtherCount: 2
# (3) One of its Options, chosen as it is gained (dragon-like/*.dbu).
options: 1
description: >
  You were created in a unique form for a purpose, to serve your progenitor.
text: >
  Dragon-like (Body): You were created in a unique form for a purpose, to serve your progenitor.
  (1)-[Passive]: Upon gaining this Factor Trait, select and gain access to up to 2 Bestial Traits. For each Bestial Trait gained, reduce your Racial Life Modifier by 1.
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase your Wound Rolls against Studied Opponents by 1(T).
  (3)-[Option]: Upon gaining this Factor Trait, select and gain access to one of the following effects:
  * Dragon Lord’s Fury [Triggered, 1/Round]: If an Ally is hit by an Attacking Maneuver from a Studied Opponent, you may use the Intervene Maneuver without spending a Counter Action.
  * Dragon Lord’s Rage [Triggered, 1/Round]: If a Studied Ally on an adjacent Square targets an Opponent with an Attacking Maneuver, you may use the United Attack Maneuver without spending an Action through its effects.

---

[passive]
# (1) Racial Life 1 down for each Bestial Trait it gave - those still held.
if (grantedOthersAtLeast(1, "dragon-like")) {
    racialLifeModifier -= 1;
}
if (grantedOthersAtLeast(2, "dragon-like")) {
    racialLifeModifier -= 1;
}
# (2) Your Wound against an Opponent you have Studied (chat.mjs dragonLikeParts).
allow dragonLike.vsStudied;
